  clock: 2  # 1011
  nonce: '1011'  # 1011
  message: "REPRODUCED AT TIP 2026-09-07 AND GIVEN ITS FIRST MEASURED VOLUME on one population, while landing WI-gamas (Phase 6 PR 4). This item's filing says \"VOLUME UNMEASURED -- no out-of-span DST count exists\"; here is one population's count, which is not the item's total but is no longer nothing.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL REPRO at dev 946ad85633, production `analyze_python` on a fixture (`~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/mumov_instwrite_09072026/fx` + `dump.py`): in a file where an UNRELATED class `Order` defines `save`, a `self.save()` inside `class Direct(models.Model)` -- which defines no `save` anywhere in its lineage -- emits a RESOLVED edge to `Order.save`. Exactly the shape this item filed, at tip, with a positive control in the same run.\n\nVOLUME ON ONE POPULATION (pretix, all `self.save()` / `self.delete()` sites, AST census): 27 resolve to the enclosing class's own method (correct), 8 reach the unresolved branch, and 2 are claimed by an unrelated same-file class of the same name -- `CustomerSSOClient.save` binding to `Customer`, and `Order.delete` binding to one of `OrderFee` / `PrintLog` / `QuestionAnswer`. So 2 of 37 on this population.\n\nWHY IT COST SOMETHING RATHER THAN BEING COSMETIC. (1) It caps the population of WI-gamas's lineage rule at 8 sites on pretix, because a site the resolver has already claimed never reaches the branch that would type it. (2) It produced a FALSE POSITIVE in measurement 0016's adjudication: `ReauthView.post`'s only new flow runs into `StopStaffSession.get`, an unrelated view class's method claimed by short name at `self.get(request, *args, **kwargs)`, and the write it reaches has nothing to do with the value read. That is 1 of the 3 false positives in a 11-situation delta, so on this measurement the item is worth about 9 points of precision.\n\nNo status change proposed and no fix attempted here; the item's own gate (\"a directed dst-blast-radius probe before implementing\") is untouched and still the right first step."  # 1011
- op: discuss  # e269
  at: '2026-09-09T04:56:37Z'  # e269
  by: agent  # e269
  actor: jgstern_agent  # e269
  clock: 3  # e269
  nonce: e269  # e269
  message: "A FURTHER INSTANCE, WITH ITS COST IN A SECOND MEASUREMENT, observed 2026-09-09 while landing WI-sihoh (Phase 6 PR 5, measurement 0021).\n\nTHE SITE. `CartPosition.update_listed_price_and_voucher` (pretix src/pretix/base/models/orders.py:3246) calls `self.save(update_fields=[...])` at 3277. `CartPosition` defines NO `save` override -- checked at source -- so that call reaches Django's own `Model.save`. The reported flow path instead runs `[update_listed_price_and_voucher, PrintLog.save]`: `PrintLog` is an unrelated model declared in the SAME FILE (orders.py:3571) whose `save` was claimed by short name. Exactly this item's mechanism.\n\n`PrintLog` is one of the three classes this item's 2026-09-07 entry already named as a candidate binding for `Order.delete`, so the class is not new to the thread; the CALLER is.\n\nA DISCREPANCY WORTH CHECKING WHEN THIS ITEM'S GATE IS WORKED, reported rather than resolved. The 2026-09-07 census over all pretix `self.save()`/`self.delete()` sites found 27 correct, 8 unresolved, and 2 claimed by an unrelated same-file class (`CustomerSSOClient.save` -> `Customer`, `Order.delete` -> one of `OrderFee`/`PrintLog`/`QuestionAnswer`). `CartPosition.update_listed_price_and_voucher` -> `PrintLog.save` is not obviously among those 2. Either the census undercounted, or the tree moved between 946ad85633 and 8127dc8245. I did not chase it; whoever runs the directed dst-blast-radius probe this item gates on should, because a census that undercounts its own population would size the fix wrong.\n\nCOST ON THIS MEASUREMENT. It is the single judgement call in 0021's adjudication of 16 situations. Under measurement 0001's rubric as written -- \"a real value flow exists from the source's value to the NAMED sink\", and the named sink is the generic `django.db.models.save` -- it is a TRUE POSITIVE with a defective evidence path, because the value genuinely does flow (`first()` -> `bundle.designated_price` -> `self.listed_price` -> `self.save()`). Under a stricter reading requiring the path to be correct end to end it is a FALSE POSITIVE, and 0021 reads 50.0% instead of 56.3%. The ship bar was met either way, so this item did not decide that PR -- but it did make one of sixteen findings unreadable without a source check.\n\nNOT the same as the 0016 instance this thread already records (`ReauthView.post` -> `StopStaffSession.get`), which was an unambiguous false positive: there the genuine write was on a loop variable that stays untyped, so the finding had no true counterpart at all. Here the genuine write is real. The two instances bracket the item's cost range.\n\nNo status change proposed; the item's gate (a directed dst-blast-radius probe before implementing) is untouched and still the right first step."  # e269
